      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: I understand that report dumps are hard to keep track of, but there's better ways of addressing these types of reports. Even simply saying \"I've scanned through your report, and it looks like a few of these are already being worked on!\" makes the reporter* feel like their voice was heard.\nSimply saying \"don't do x\" might deters the poster, and future posters from bothering to call out bugs. Saying; \"I've read your report\", \"thank you for your time\", and \"please submit separate posts to help us\" makes an individual feel important, and meaningful when reporting these issues.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-11-01T16:21:18.570Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I decided to make a big report dumb with all the issues I encounter on daily basis. \nHope this helps getting everything patched up. \n1. Fully body jitters/ spazzes out when walking on sloped surfaces ( https://youtu.be/y6VwqMcgLXI )\nThis makes walking with full body very uncomfortable and standing on any sloped surface just causes issues. \nIntroduced in the 3.0 update\nThings I tried to fix it: \nRemoving the falling animation from the base controller, Turning off locomotion animations for 6 point tracking.\nSeems like it has to do something with the falling animation triggering over and over but Removing them didnt seem to fix the issue.\n2. Friends list shows as empty upon first opening social menu, Menu needs to be closed and than opened again for the list to actually display.\n3. When joining a new world theres a chance nobodys avatar will load. \nIntroduced in VRChat 2020.4.1, build number 1004\n4. Avatar 3.0 animations will not show for other players unless you re-calibrate right in front of them.\nIntroduced in VRChat 2020.4.1, build number 1004\n5. World master/host will have a laggy voice/ repeat the same part of a word over and over for seconds or minutes after. \nIntroduced in VRChat 2020.4.1p3, build 1007\n6. Game unexpectedly crashes after 20 or so minutes.\nI am running 32gb of ram so its probably not due to a memory leak.\nIntroduced in VRChat 2020.4.1p3, build 1007\nThere was a fix in build 1008\nbut that one didnt seem to fix it completely \n7. Camera need a complete redesign. This is an ancient issue and I am confused why it was never addressed. Camera buttons are very hard to hit from most angles.\n8. Vote kicking sometimes doesnt work. Even if everyone in the world agrees to kick someone they still dont get kicked. \nI am really hoping this helps track issues down and fix them. Sadly some of these issues go under the rug and never get fixed or bake even more in the future. \nI am still behind the fact that a lot of the recent updates have caused more problems than they have fixed. I dont know if this was caused because of a lack of playtesters but the past few days have really not been enjoyable in  vrchat for one reason or another.",
